                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "00ef86e1-eace-34b3-9a4a-1189ef239b58",
                        "entry_id": "c9ae4702-b531-3f78-9238-277ce51bd2bd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "поэт. или высок. рассматривать, наблюдать кого-либо, что-либо"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "015f4eaf-41db-4260-9f0d-95fa31cef26e",
                                "sense_id": "00ef86e1-eace-34b3-9a4a-1189ef239b58",
                                "text": "Я не могу долго созерцать море и лес и, если не вправду разгуляться, то хотя бы вообразить, поласкать себя возможностью принять личное участие в этой великой картине."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "42290857-a049-37c5-a914-5f0f6e122ba9",
                        "entry_id": "c9ae4702-b531-3f78-9238-277ce51bd2bd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен. мысленно представлять"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "296840a8-435f-4243-9b11-d2f91924a000",
                        "source_entry_id": "c9ae4702-b531-3f78-9238-277ce51bd2bd",
                        "target_lang_word": "contemplate",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "contemplate",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6f997927-2d61-3835-922d-af27756e19cb",
                                        "entry_id": "b68c6b26-d95e-382f-b33a-97bcc8bef5ac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To look at on all sides or in all its aspects; to view or consider with continued attention; to regard with deliberate care; to meditate on; to study, ponder, or consider."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b303ed5-937d-44cc-8635-2fa258e8e01a",
                                                "sense_id": "6f997927-2d61-3835-922d-af27756e19cb",
                                                "text": "To love, at least contemplate and admire, / What I see excellent."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "792c1bac-c62e-4a2c-a8c4-c0cf845d1939",
                                                "sense_id": "6f997927-2d61-3835-922d-af27756e19cb",
                                                "text": "We thus dilate / Our spirits to the size of that they contemplate."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a36cb22e-3252-330e-9bb7-9adce247faab",
                                        "entry_id": "b68c6b26-d95e-382f-b33a-97bcc8bef5ac",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To consider as a possibility."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "096d3416-853c-4b98-8138-b00a18144ac1",
                                                "sense_id": "a36cb22e-3252-330e-9bb7-9adce247faab",
                                                "text": "I contemplated doing the project myself, but it would have taken too long."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8bd4ba2b-379c-41f9-82a7-9406e09aaa51",
                                                "sense_id": "a36cb22e-3252-330e-9bb7-9adce247faab",
                                                "text": "There remain some particulars to complete the information contemplated by those resolutions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f5c36cb6-cde0-409c-a7ea-22ccf18e47c9",
                                                "sense_id": "a36cb22e-3252-330e-9bb7-9adce247faab",
                                                "text": "If a treaty contains any stipulations which contemplate a state of future war."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "95fd6fcb-4011-48d9-b945-3a9ddc15c732",
                                                "sense_id": "a36cb22e-3252-330e-9bb7-9adce247faab",
                                                "text": "In Calcutta, season tickets are issued only for the calendar month, with a different colour for each month, so that this problem does not arise. The merest whisper of an idea to change Bombay to the Calcutta system brought such a howl of protest in the Press, that it was never seriously contemplated."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1fbefeba-61ae-4d6f-b6ed-d2288c1e5025",
                                                "sense_id": "a36cb22e-3252-330e-9bb7-9adce247faab",
                                                "text": "Since the launch early last year of […] two Silicon Valley start-ups offering free education through MOOCs, massive open online courses, the ivory towers of academia have been shaken to their foundations. University brands built in some cases over centuries have been forced to contemplate the possibility that information technology will rapidly make their existing business model obsolete."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5fe8d67b-c7e5-47b7-9f70-9c9a19116a51",
                        "source_entry_id": "c9ae4702-b531-3f78-9238-277ce51bd2bd",
                        "target_lang_word": "observe",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "observe",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c908fd7c-27a6-3ee1-88bb-9646a8aaa653",
                                        "entry_id": "a404216a-c592-3fc6-b705-4d0bc9218b3a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To notice or view, especially carefully or with attention to detail."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9085012b-0c85-46b9-af79-4a26abdde4ef",
                                                "sense_id": "c908fd7c-27a6-3ee1-88bb-9646a8aaa653",
                                                "text": "From this vantage point we can observe the behavior of the animals in their natural habitat."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3685aa0a-cb67-4d36-8f1d-c8cc7240fe9b",
                                                "sense_id": "c908fd7c-27a6-3ee1-88bb-9646a8aaa653",
                                                "text": "She got up before dawn to observe the lunar eclipse."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d0969281-f939-4183-a3c8-0d4494a83516",
                                                "sense_id": "c908fd7c-27a6-3ee1-88bb-9646a8aaa653",
                                                "text": "“One horse?” interjected Holmes. ¶ “Yes, only one.” ¶ “Did you observe the colour?”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ff4e11e-b0ae-41a9-8787-7096c71b902e",
                                                "sense_id": "c908fd7c-27a6-3ee1-88bb-9646a8aaa653",
                                                "text": "An extreme version of vorticity is a vortex. The vortex is a spinning, cyclonic mass of fluid, which can be observed in the rotation of water going down a drain, as well as in smoke rings, tornados and hurricanes."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f9a97e40-02cd-3de7-b615-ebd920e1452b",
                                        "entry_id": "a404216a-c592-3fc6-b705-4d0bc9218b3a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To follow or obey the custom, practice, or rules (especially of a religion)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a81aa59e-9dc9-404e-a713-bf6a14d0e7df",
                                                "sense_id": "f9a97e40-02cd-3de7-b615-ebd920e1452b",
                                                "text": "Please observe all posted speed limits."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "46111786-34f9-4363-b60e-1900686a42c2",
                                                "sense_id": "f9a97e40-02cd-3de7-b615-ebd920e1452b",
                                                "text": "Some of them have, in fact, given them a theoretical elaboration which for subtlety, refinement, and elegance need make no apologies to the older economics, and which remains faithful to older theorizing in at least one respect, that the tradition of unintelligibility to the layman is scrupulously observed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d3a962b3-05e2-46d4-a42e-f46c54a8cab8",
                                                "sense_id": "f9a97e40-02cd-3de7-b615-ebd920e1452b",
                                                "text": "A sell-out crowd of 10,000 then observed perfectly a period of silence before the team revealed their black armbands, complete with stitched-in poppies, for the match. After Fifa’s about-turn, it must have been a frantic few days for the England kit manufacturer. The on-field challenge was altogether more straightforward."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3aa33011-97de-3a32-9809-25ecb4b21230",
                                        "entry_id": "a404216a-c592-3fc6-b705-4d0bc9218b3a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To take note of and celebrate (a holiday or similar occurrence), to keep; to follow (a type of time or calendar reckoning)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6a376eeb-5c98-4572-8a0a-71b1c07c7d7a",
                                                "sense_id": "3aa33011-97de-3a32-9809-25ecb4b21230",
                                                "text": "Ye shall observe the feast of unleavened bread."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd33f8fa-4a2b-4472-8893-c6166776325d",
                                                "sense_id": "3aa33011-97de-3a32-9809-25ecb4b21230",
                                                "text": "On Sunday, most of Canada will observe daylight time and spring forward an hour in order to reflect the increasing sunlight."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "963f8061-dd65-3174-b56e-0fc54657a931",
                                        "entry_id": "a404216a-c592-3fc6-b705-4d0bc9218b3a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To comment on something; to make an observation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "195c8390-0452-4711-b349-d8759b88bd9a",
                                                "sense_id": "963f8061-dd65-3174-b56e-0fc54657a931",
                                                "text": "The senator observed that the bill would be detrimental to his constituents."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d650e0fd-1459-47cf-8695-d2f99eb925ac",
                                                "sense_id": "963f8061-dd65-3174-b56e-0fc54657a931",
                                                "text": "Elbows almost touching they leaned at ease, idly reading the almost obliterated lines engraved there. ¶ \"I never understood it,\" she observed, lightly scornful. \"What occult meaning has a sun-dial for the spooney? I'm sure I don't want to read riddles in a strange gentleman's optics.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "observe",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e6a7e559-c5ce-3726-a99e-459893b19c52",
                                        "entry_id": "c115bee1-d5f3-3fb3-9896-9a60b77a74fb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An observation (remark, comment or judgement)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "890a98f3-39d5-48ea-8062-8608e2b86476",
                                                "sense_id": "e6a7e559-c5ce-3726-a99e-459893b19c52",
                                                "text": "“It sticks in my mind that he would take it very ill,” says Alan. “But the little man cried to me to run, and indeed I thought it was a good observe, and ran. The last that I saw they were all in a knot upon the beach, like folk that were not agreeing very well together.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
